<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Engage &mdash; Literary Science</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 8rem 3rem 2.5rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .page-header h1 {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  .page-header .page-desc {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--warm-gray); max-width: 500px;
  }

  .offerings {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
  }

  .offering {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 300px 1fr;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    transition: background 0.4s;
  }

  .offering:hover { background: var(--paper-light); }

  .offering-left {
    padding: 3rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
  }

  .offering-num {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 3rem; font-weight: 700;
    opacity: 0.05; line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .offering-title {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .offering-tag {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .offering-right {
    padding: 3rem;
  }

  .offering-body {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    max-width: 520px;
  }

  .offering-body + .offering-body { margin-top: 1rem; }

  .offering-formats {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .format-tag {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    color: var(--faded);
  }

  .offering-cta {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .offering-cta a {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.52rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 0.6rem 1.4rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    transition: all 0.3s;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .offering-cta a:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  /* contact strip */
  .contact-strip {
    padding: 4rem 3rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    text-align: center;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .contact-strip::before, .contact-strip::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute;
    top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 20px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom,
      transparent 0px, transparent 3px,
      rgba(242,242,242,0.03) 3px, rgba(242,242,242,0.03) 4px);
  }
  .contact-strip::before { left: 0; }
  .contact-strip::after { right: 0; }

  .contact-strip h2 {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .contact-strip p {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--paper-dark);
    max-width: 480px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .contact-strip a {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    padding: 0.7rem 1.6rem;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    transition: all 0.3s;
  }

  .contact-strip a:hover {
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .offering { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .offering-left { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-dark); padding: 2rem 1.5rem; }
    .offering-right { padding: 2rem 1.5rem; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <a href="/" class="nav-logo">Literary Science</a>
  <ul class="nav-links">
    <li><a href="/epistemology/">The Work</a></li>
    <li><a href="/studio/">Studio</a></li>
    <li><a href="/toolkit/">Toolkit</a></li>
    <li><a href="/work/" class="active">Engage</a></li>
    <li><a href="/newcomm/">NewComm</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

<header class="page-header">
  <div class="section-label">04 &mdash; The Door</div>
  <h1>Engage</h1>
  <p class="page-desc">Your campus, your museum, your library is an asset your community doesn&rsquo;t have access to. Literary Science is the methodology that transforms what that space is for.</p>
</header>

<div class="offerings">

  <div class="offering reveal">
    <div class="offering-left">
      <div class="offering-num">01</div>
      <div class="offering-title">Discovery</div>
      <div class="offering-tag">The Starting Point</div>
    </div>
    <div class="offering-right">
      <p class="offering-body">We come in. We observe your current programming, meet your people, understand your community context, and read the space&mdash;what assets are inside the gate, what potential is unrealized, and what Literary Science would look like in your specific environment. You receive a written assessment and an implementation roadmap.</p>
      <p class="offering-body">This is for institutions that sense something needs to change but aren&rsquo;t sure what the change looks like. Discovery gives you a clear picture before you commit.</p>
      <div class="offering-formats">
        <span class="format-tag">Site Assessment</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Stakeholder Interviews</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Implementation Roadmap</span>
      </div>
      <div class="offering-cta">
        <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Start Here &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="offering reveal">
    <div class="offering-left">
      <div class="offering-num">02</div>
      <div class="offering-title">Training &amp; Residency</div>
      <div class="offering-tag">Building Capacity</div>
    </div>
    <div class="offering-right">
      <p class="offering-body">We train your teachers, facilitators, and program leaders in the Literary Science methodology&mdash;how to select texts, how to teach through the lens of systems analysis, how to connect literary analysis to community data, how to facilitate hypothesis development. This can include a site visit to NewComm, where Literary Science was born and is practiced at its fullest.</p>
      <p class="offering-body">The goal is not dependence on an outside consultant. It is building your institution&rsquo;s internal capacity to practice Literary Science on your own terms, with your own community, using your own texts.</p>
      <div class="offering-formats">
        <span class="format-tag">Faculty Workshops</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Multi-Day Intensive</span>
        <span class="format-tag">NewComm Site Visit</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Ongoing Coaching</span>
      </div>
      <div class="offering-cta">
        <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Inquire &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="offering reveal">
    <div class="offering-left">
      <div class="offering-num">03</div>
      <div class="offering-title">Institutional Redesign</div>
      <div class="offering-tag">The Deepest Engagement</div>
    </div>
    <div class="offering-right">
      <p class="offering-body">This is not a workshop about the methodology. It is the methodology built into your institution&rsquo;s architecture. We work with you over a full year to reimagine your space&mdash;transforming it from a site of traditional programming into a site of collective knowledge-making, community investment, and shared power.</p>
      <p class="offering-body">For schools, museums, libraries, and cultural institutions ready to ask the harder question: not how do we serve the community, but what becomes possible when we open the gate and build together?</p>
      <div class="offering-formats">
        <span class="format-tag">Program Design</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Curriculum Integration</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Space Reimagination</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Supported Implementation</span>
      </div>
      <div class="offering-cta">
        <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Start a Conversation &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="offering reveal">
    <div class="offering-left">
      <div class="offering-num">04</div>
      <div class="offering-title">Certification</div>
      <div class="offering-tag">First Cohort &mdash; 2027</div>
    </div>
    <div class="offering-right">
      <p class="offering-body">A structured pathway for educators, community organizers, museum professionals, and curriculum designers who want to practice Literary Science independently. Learn the methodology. Teach it. Contribute to its evolution. Certification means you can facilitate Literary Science in your own context, with your own community, using your own texts.</p>
      <div class="offering-formats">
        <span class="format-tag">Practitioner</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Resident</span>
        <span class="format-tag">Fellow</span>
      </div>
      <div class="offering-cta">
        <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Join the Waitlist &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="contact-strip reveal">
  <h2>Let&rsquo;s talk.</h2>
  <p>Whether you&rsquo;re a school ready to reimagine what your campus is for, a museum exploring how to activate your space for community good, or an organization that wants Literary Science in your context&mdash;it starts with a conversation.</p>
  <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">hello@literaryscience.com</a>
</div>

<footer>
  <div class="footer-left">Literary Science</div>
  <div class="footer-right">A property of Asoluka LLC &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <a href="#">Contact</a> &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; &copy; 2026</div>
</footer>

<script>
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(e => { if (e.isIntersecting) e.target.classList.add('visible'); });
  }, { threshold: 0.1 });
  document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
</script>
</body>
</html>
